menu "Claw BLE Scan Capability"

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_SCAN_MAX_RESULTS
    int "Max devices retained per scan"
    default 32
    range 8 128
    help
        Upper bound on the number of distinct BLE devices retained in one
        scan window. Beyond this limit further advertising packets are
        dropped and the result JSON sets truncated=true. Higher values
        cost ~96 bytes of heap per entry.

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_SCAN_DEFAULT_DURATION_MS
    int "Default scan duration (ms)"
    default 5000
    range 500 60000
    help
        Default window length used when the LLM does not specify
        duration_ms in the call input. Clamped to [500, 60000] at
        runtime regardless of this setting.

config CLAW_CAP_BLE_SCAN_PASSIVE
    bool "Use passive scanning by default"
    default y
    help
        Passive scan only listens; active scan also issues SCAN_REQ to
        peers that advertise scannable PDUs (gets richer name / mfg data
        but is detectable and a bit more power-hungry). Per-call override
        is exposed via the "active" input field.

endmenu
